>> title: Spinach and Bacon Quiche
>> servings: 8
>> source: https://tastesbetterfromscratch.com/spinach-and-bacon-quiche 


== Blind Bake Crust ==

> Note: this recipe assumes you already have Pie Dough. 

Preheat the oven to 375 F. Roll out one disc of @./miscellaneous/Pie Dough{} into a circle, 12 inches in diameter. Place in a #9-inch glass pie plate{} and crimp edges.

Place a piece of #parchment paper{} inside the pie pan and add 2 cups of #pie weights{}, dry beans or rice. 

Bake at 375 F for ~{15%minutes} then remove parchment paper and pie weights. 

Prick pie crust all over with a fork, then return to the oven for ~{8%minutes}.

== Assembly ==

Cook @bacon{6%slices}(cooked and crumbled) in a #skillet{}. Once cooked, remove to a plate and chop. 

Remove most of the grease from the pan and add @onion{1/2}(chopped) and @baby spinach leaves{1.5%cups}(loosely measured, then chopped). Sauté for ~{2%minutes}. 

Add @cheese{1.25%cups}(shredded), onion, spinach, and bacon to the bottom of the partially baked pie crust.

Combine @eggs{5}(beaten), @half & half{1.25%cups}, @salt{}, and @black pepper{} in a #blender{}, then pour the egg mixture into the pie.

Reduce oven temperature to 350 F. Bake quiche for ~{40-45%minutes} until the egg mixture is set. 

Allow to cool for ~{10%minutes}, or even to room temperature, before slicing. Store leftovers, covered, in the fridge.